        "title": "refactor(plugins): trim registry exports",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe plugin-registry decomposition in #105783 exposed ten owner-private symbols that Knip immediately reported as unused exports. One path helper also remained baseline-allowlisted solely for direct internal tests.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n- Delete seven unused registrar return-type aliases.\n- Privatize the registration-capability type and hook-timeout normalizer.\n- Remove the stale `resolvePluginPath` barrel export and dead-export baseline entry.\n- Move path-resolution assertions onto the supported `OpenClawPluginApi.resolvePath` surface.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo runtime behavior or public Plugin SDK contract changes. Plugin path resolution retains the same relative, absolute, and home-path behavior.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Fresh Testbox `pnpm deadcode:exports`: baseline matched 5,708 entries.\n- Fresh Testbox focused suite: 2 files, 32 tests passed.\n- Fresh Testbox targeted `check:changed`: passed in 10m45s.\n- Fresh committed-branch `gpt-5.6-sol` medium autoreview: no findings, patch correct at 0.93 confidence.\n- `git diff --check` passes.\n- Net reduction: 27 additions, 41 deletions across 13 files.\n\nNo changelog entry: this is an internal export cleanup with unchanged runtime behavior.\n",
